{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Fix + measurements (local, quiet machine, `-p no:randomly`, whole module).\n\n| | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| module wall | 50.14s | **5.96s** (-88%) |\n| module CPU (user+sys) | 46.13s | **6.24s** (-86%) |\n| the four guards | 11.87 + 11.85 + 11.83 + 10.90 = **46.45s** | one 4.14s fill + ~0.02s each |\n\n`_run_request_sites` invocation count, measured with a temporary pytest plugin that wraps the function and reports at session finish: **1** (was 4). AC met exactly.\n\nThe two layers separate cleanly in the numbers. Layer 1 (the filed concern, four repeats) accounts for the 4 -> 1 drop. Layer 2 (the per-path parse memo) shows up in the size of a SINGLE scan: 11.83s per call before, 4.14s after — **-65% on one scan**, because `_verdict` no longer re-reads and re-parses the whole tree once per parameter-provenance site and `_functions` no longer parses it again.\n\nEquivalence proven, not assumed. The origin/main version of the module and the changed version were both loaded in place and their `_run_request_sites()` output dumped to JSON:\n\n    sites before: 24  after: 24\n    IDENTICAL (order + content): True\n\nSo all 24 `(key, expr, verdict)` tuples are unchanged in value AND order; no assertion body or offender message was edited, only the parameter each test receives.\n\nDefect seeding: a `_seeded_defect_probe` was added to `src/rebar/llm/enrich.py` building `RunRequest(config=cfg, ...)` from `LLMConfig.from_env()`. Through the cached path the guard still catches it by name:\n\n    E   AssertionError: these RunRequest sites inherit cfg.model instead of selecting a model class (bug afeb): {'llm/enrich.py::_seeded_defect_probe': 'cfg'}\n    FAILED tests/unit/test_subcall_class_selection.py::test_no_run_request_inherits_the_raw_config_model\n\nReverted immediately; `git status` shows only the test file modified.\n\nCross-session staleness: nothing is written to disk. The cache is a pytest session fixture plus a `functools.cache` on `_parsed`, both of which die with the process, so a later session cannot be served a pre-change analysis. `src/rebar` is read-only to this suite, and the module's only autouse fixture patches `llm_config._read_llm_file_table`, which the AST scan never consults.\n\nGates: 11 `check_*` pass, complexity `new=0 increased=0 stale=0`, lint and typecheck clean."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786608601859062001,"uuid":"84733f15-2e87-424a-895e-e7df2fba04b3"}